1
00:01:17,034 --> 00:01:19,620
♪♪ [ Woman Vocalizing ]

2
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:41,558
♪♪ [ Vocalizing Continues ]

3
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:07,793
[ Computer Voice ] Stasis interrupted.
Fire in cryogenic compartment.

4
00:02:07,878 --> 00:02:12,381
Repeat.
Fire in cryogenic compartment.

5
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:15,384
All personnel report to...

6
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:18,179
emergency escape vehicle.

7
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:23,016
Launch of the escape lifeboat
will commence...

8
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:27,021
in T-minus 20 seconds.

9
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:40,784
[ Siren Wailing ]

10
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:52,921
♪♪ [ Vocalizing Continues ]

11
00:03:43,307 --> 00:03:46,516
[ Breathing Heavily ]

12
00:03:46,602 --> 00:03:49,645
[ Alarm Blaring ]

13
00:03:57,695 --> 00:04:00,907
♪♪ [ Vocalizing Continues ]

14
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:38,778
[ Wind Gusting ]

15
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:44,824
[ Chains Clanking ]

16
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:05,721
[ Bell Tolls ]

17
00:06:24,259 --> 00:06:27,386
An E.E.V.'s come down.

18
00:06:27,471 --> 00:06:29,555
Get down to the beach.
There may be others.

19
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,848
Now!

20
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:47,947
Talk to me.

21
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,951
Come on. Come on.

22
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:56,540
[ Grunts ]

23
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:15,266
[ Lows ]
Hey, Frank! Come on! Let's go!
Let's go!

24
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:17,019
Wait!

25
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:20,773
[ Typing ]

26
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:52,303
[ Electricity Crackling ]

27
00:07:58,185 --> 00:08:00,187
[ Groans ]

28
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:45,191
[ Man ]
Get goin', Frank. Get in there.

29
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:48,152
[ Man #2 ]
Oh! Jesus Christ!

30
00:08:48,235 --> 00:08:50,613
[ Man #3 ]
Hell of a way to make a landing!

31
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:53,198
[ Man #4 ]
Use the torch.

32
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:58,077
How many?
Don't know.

33
00:08:58,163 --> 00:08:59,996
Three. Maybe four.

34
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:04,335
Hey, Frank. Can we hurry this up?
It's gonna be 40 below in five minutes.

35
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:06,879
[ Wind Gusting ]

36
00:09:29,693 --> 00:09:33,029
All right, all right.
Let's get it going.

37
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:36,575
Keep it together.
Come on. Right.

38
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,994
Right. Here we go, Mr. Dillon.

39
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:49,922
Give us strength,
O Lord, to endure.

40
00:09:50,005 --> 00:09:54,217
We recognize that we are poor sinners
in the hands of an angry God.

41
00:09:55,552 --> 00:09:57,846
Let the circle be unbroken...

42
00:09:57,931 --> 00:10:00,014
until the day.

43
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:07,022
- Amen.
- [ All ]
Amen.

44
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:15,990
Thank you, gentlemen.
This is rumor control.

45
00:10:16,073 --> 00:10:18,616
Here are the facts.

46
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:21,202
As some of you know,

47
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:24,664
a 337 model E.E.V....

48
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:27,960
crash-landed here at 0600...

49
00:10:28,043 --> 00:10:30,629
on the morning watch.

50
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:33,256
There was one survivor,

51
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:37,720
two dead and a droid that was
hopelessly smashed beyond repair.

52
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:40,389
The survivor is a woman.

53
00:10:40,472 --> 00:10:42,807
[ Chattering, Laughing ]

54
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:44,058
[ Man ]
That's what I saw.

55
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:46,687
I just want to say that I've taken
a vow of celibacy.

56
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:49,063
[ Man #2 ]
So have we all.
That also includes women.

57
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,274
Yes.
We've all taken the vow!

58
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,028
[ Man #3 ] Shut your gob, Morse.
[ Morse ]
I'd like to say that I, for one,

59
00:10:54,111 --> 00:10:56,613
do not appreciate company policy
allowing her to freely...

60
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:58,823
intermingle with inmates
and the rest of the staff.

61
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:03,578
What brother means to say is we view
the presence of any outsider,

62
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:08,292
especially a woman,
as a violation of the harmony,

63
00:11:08,375 --> 00:11:10,293
a potential break
in the spiritual unity.

64
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:13,004
We are well aware
of your feelings in this matter.

65
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:17,717
You will be pleased to know
that I have requested a rescue team.

66
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,386
Hopefully, they will be here
inside of a week-

67
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:24,557
Oh, come on!
and evacuate her A.S.A.P.

68
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,559
[ Man ]
Don't give us that!

69
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:28,519
What's her medical status?

70
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:30,522
She doesn't seem
too badly damaged.

71
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:34,442
She's unconscious. Can't give you
a more specific diagnosis at the moment.

72
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:36,903
- Will she live?
- I would think so.

73
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,657
Look. It's in
everybody's interest...

74
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:44,452
the woman doesn't come out of the infirmary
until the rescue team arrives.

75
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:48,706
And certainly not without
an escort, right?
Sir.

76
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:54,296
Gentlemen, we should all stick
to our set routine...

77
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,548
and not get unduly agitated.

78
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,133
Right.
Correct?

79
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:02,096
All right.
Thank you, gentlemen.

80
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,640
[ Sighs ]

81
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,394
All right.

82
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,188
[ Man ]
Better get here soon
or there ain't gonna be much left.

83
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:42,635
[ Clattering ]

84
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:51,061
[ lnhales Sharply ]
What's that?

85
00:12:52,312 --> 00:12:56,357
It's just a little cocktail of my own mix.
Sort of eye-opener.

86
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,860
[ Breathing Heavily ]
You a doctor?

87
00:12:58,945 --> 00:13:02,489
My name is Clemens.
I'm the chief medical officer here.

88
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:05,616
Here?
Fury 161.

89
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:09,078
It's one of Weyland-Yutani's
backwater work prisons,

90
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:11,081
it grieves me to say.

91
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:13,082
Do you mind?

92
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:18,797
This is basically a stabilizer.

93
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:21,799
I really ought to shave your head.

94
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,385
We have a big problem with lice here.

95
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:26,971
And when you're feeling better,
I'll give you some clippers,

96
00:13:27,097 --> 00:13:31,100
and you can tend to
your private parts yourself.
How'd I get here?

97
00:13:32,644 --> 00:13:36,230
You crash-landed in an E.E.V.

98
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:39,817
Evidently separated from your mother ship
before you hit our atmosphere.

99
00:13:39,903 --> 00:13:43,238
You have any idea
how long you were in hypersleep?

100
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,948
'Cause coming out the way you did
can be quite a jolt to the system.

101
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,534
Yeah, I'll be sick for a couple of weeks.
Indeed.

102
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:52,371
[ Sighs ]

103
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:55,375
- Where are the others?
- They didn't make it.

104
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,544
- What?
- They didn't survive.

105
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,634
I have to get to the ship.

106
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:07,803
- Have to get to the ship.
- You're in no condition for that.

107
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:11,767
You want to get me some clothes,
or should I just go like this?

108
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:16,687
Given the nature of our indigenous population,
I would suggest clothes.

109
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:21,652
- [ Clears Throat ]
- None of them
have seen a woman in years.

110
00:14:24,279 --> 00:14:26,615
Neither have I, for that matter.

111
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:32,328
This used to be
a 5,000 convict facility,

112
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:36,040
but it's been reduced
to a custodial staff of 25.

113
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,084
Why?

114
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:39,168
Keep the pilot light on.
The pilot light for what?

115
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:44,841
[ Shouting ]
Blast furnace. Natural methane.

116
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:48,552
We have a foundry,
Lieutenant Ripley.

117
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:52,014
The inmates forge lead sheets
for toxic waste containers.

118
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,850
How do you know my name?

119
00:14:54,936 --> 00:14:57,729
It's stenciled
on the back of your shorts.

120
00:14:57,813 --> 00:15:01,357
[ Men Shouting, Indistinct ]

121
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:09,283
[ Man ]
Release the cable!

122
00:15:26,341 --> 00:15:28,884
Where are the bodies?
We have a morgue.

123
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:32,931
We put them there
until the investigative team arrives
in about a week, I think.

124
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:35,475
[ Clattering ]

125
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:39,270
There was a droid.
Disconnected.

126
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:41,856
There were bits and pieces of him
all over the place.

127
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:44,025
We put what was left
on the rubbish tip.

128
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:47,486
The corporal was impaled
by that safety support.

129
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:49,530
He never knew what hit him.

130
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,991
And the girl?

131
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:55,412
She drowned in her cryo-tube.

132
00:15:55,495 --> 00:15:59,915
I don't think she was conscious
when it happened.

133
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,169
Um, I'm sorry.

134
00:16:03,254 --> 00:16:06,005
[ Sobbing ]

135
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,049
[ Exhales ]

136
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,774
[ Gasps ]
What's the matter?

137
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:28,278
Where is she?
In the morgue.

138
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:30,279
I have to see her.

139
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:33,616
I have to see what's left of her.

140
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:36,827
[ Door Opens ]

141
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:42,667
Is there any particular reason
that you're so insistent?

142
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:46,879
Yes. I have to be sure
how she died.

143
00:16:46,963 --> 00:16:50,049
I hate to be repetitious
about such a sensitive subject,

144
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:54,261
but it is persectly clear
that she drowned.

145
00:16:58,558 --> 00:17:00,559
Was she your daughter?

146
00:17:02,897 --> 00:17:05,941
No. She wasn't.

147
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:47,816
Um-

148
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,317
C-Could I have a moment
alone, please?

149
00:17:50,403 --> 00:17:52,362
Yes, of course.

150
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,795
[ Sighs ]

151
00:18:25,563 --> 00:18:27,564
[ Softly ]
Forgive me.

152
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:54,382
What's she doing?

153
00:19:06,394 --> 00:19:08,896
Okay?

154
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:11,191
No.

155
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:14,152
We have to do an autopsy.

156
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:15,987
What?
I told you,

157
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:18,323
we have to make sure
how she died.

158
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:23,036
And I told you, she drowned.

159
00:19:23,119 --> 00:19:28,666
I'm not so sure.
I-I have to see inside of her.

160
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:31,169
You're disorientated.
Half your system's still in-

161
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:33,255
I have a very,
very good reason.

162
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:35,423
Well, perhaps you'd like to
share that reason.

163
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:41,555
Possible contagion.

164
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:44,516
What kind exactly?

165
00:19:44,599 --> 00:19:46,601
- Cholera.
- Cholera?

166
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,232
There hasn't been a case of cholera
reported for 200 years.

167
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:01,825
Please.

168
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:11,792
[ Water Gurgling ]

169
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,298
[ Cutting Skin ]

170
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:31,145
[ Yawns ]

171
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,323
Everything's in place.

172
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:44,784
There's no sign of infection.

173
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:47,578
No indication of disease.
Chest.

174
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:49,623
Open the chest.

175
00:20:58,007 --> 00:21:00,133
Careful.

176
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:15,981
[ Bones Cracking ]

177
00:21:21,364 --> 00:21:23,698
[ Sobbing ]

178
00:21:31,539 --> 00:21:33,833
Lungs.

179
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:38,212
Flooded with fluid.

180
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:42,342
Ergo, she drowned.

181
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:53,310
Now, since I'm not
a complete idiot,

182
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:57,231
would you like to tell me
what we're really looking for?

183
00:22:06,157 --> 00:22:08,492
Mr. Clemens.

184
00:22:08,576 --> 00:22:10,494
Superintendent.

185
00:22:12,163 --> 00:22:15,583
I don't believe you've met
Lieutenant Ripley.

186
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:17,669
What's going on, Mr. Clemens?

187
00:22:17,752 --> 00:22:19,878
That's right, sir.
What's going on, Mr. Clemens?

188
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:23,258
Well, first-
[ Clattering ]

189
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:28,179
the lieutenant is feeling much better,
I'm happy to say.

190
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:30,723
Second, in the interest
of public health,

191
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,518
I am performing an autopsy.
Without my authority.

192
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:36,019
Well, there didn't
seem to be time.

193
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:37,980
But it's turned out all right.

194
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:40,525
There's no sign of contagion in the body.
Good.

195
00:22:40,608 --> 00:22:44,362
But it might be helpful if Lt. Ripley
didn't parade around in front of the prisoners,

196
00:22:44,447 --> 00:22:46,573
as I am told she did in the last hour.

197
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,575
It might also be helpful...

198
00:22:48,659 --> 00:22:51,702
if you kept me informed as to
any change in her physical status.

199
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:54,163
Or would that be asking too much?

200
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:59,669
- We have to cremate the bodies.
- Nonsense. We'll keep the bodies on ice
till the rescue team arrives.

201
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:04,132
- On ice.
- There is the public health issue.

202
00:23:04,215 --> 00:23:09,220
The lieutenant feels that there is still
a possibility of a communicable infection.

203
00:23:11,307 --> 00:23:13,557
I thought you said
there was no sign of disease.

204
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,769
[ Clemens ]
It would appear that the child drowned.

205
00:23:15,853 --> 00:23:18,395
But without the benefit
of proper laboratory tests,

206
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,397
it's impossible
to be absolutely certain.

207
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:22,733
I would consider it unwise...

208
00:23:22,817 --> 00:23:26,570
to tolerate even the possibility
of an unwelcome virus.

209
00:23:26,654 --> 00:23:31,116
An outbreak of cholera
would look extremely bad on a report.

210
00:23:31,242 --> 00:23:33,536
Would it not, sir?
[ Clears Throat ]

211
00:23:34,872 --> 00:23:37,624
We've 25 prisoners in this facility.

212
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:39,792
All double-y-chromos.

213
00:23:39,876 --> 00:23:44,087
All thieves, rapists,
murderers, child molesters. All scum.

214
00:23:44,173 --> 00:23:48,926
Just because they've taken on religion
doesn't make them any less dangerous.

215
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:51,429
I try not to offend their convictions.

216
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:54,015
I don't want to upset the order.

217
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:57,602
I don't want ripples in the water.

218
00:23:57,685 --> 00:24:02,690
And I don't want a woman walking around
giving them ideas.

219
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:06,819
I see. For my own personal safety.

220
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,948
Exactly.

221
00:24:10,031 --> 00:24:14,661
I will leave the details of the cremation
to you, Mr. Clemens.

222
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:21,084
They may use the furnace, but I want
everyone back in lockup by 2200 hours.

223
00:24:21,167 --> 00:24:23,211
[ Assistant ]
You called it, sir.

224
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:32,511
[ Animal Grunting ]

225
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:52,740
Ah, Christmas
has come early, Murph.
What do you mean?

226
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:56,827
- Any dead ox is a good ox.
- You're bloody right.

227
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:59,163
Smelly bastards, all covered in lice.

228
00:24:59,248 --> 00:25:03,250
There's only seven of the friggin' things left,
and then we're done with them.

229
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:05,627
God, I hates hosin'
these bastards down.

230
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:08,172
I always get shite
all over me boots.

231
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:11,425
Talkin' of hosing
things down, Frank-
Yeah?

232
00:25:11,509 --> 00:25:14,095
You had the chance,
what would you say to her?

233
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:16,388
- What do you mean,
if I got the chance?
- You know.

234
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:19,308
If you got the chance.
You mean, casual like?

235
00:25:19,393 --> 00:25:23,645
Yeah. I mean, how would you
put it to her if you bumped into her
in the mess hall or somewhere?

236
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,606
No problem!

237
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:29,777
I've never had any problem
with the ladies.

238
00:25:29,862 --> 00:25:32,779
I'd say to her, "Good day, my dear.
How's it goin'?

239
00:25:32,865 --> 00:25:35,450
Anything I can do to be of service?"

240
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:38,536
Then I'd give her the look,
you know- up and down.
[ Grunts ]

241
00:25:38,621 --> 00:25:41,955
And I'd give her the wink,
the dirty smile.

242
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:44,541
She'd soon get the picture.
Yeah, right.

243
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:48,296
And then she'd say,
"Kiss my ass, you horny old fucker!"

244
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:51,048
I'd be happy to kiss her ass.

245
00:25:51,133 --> 00:25:54,093
I'd be happy to kiss her
anywhere she wants.
[ Smacks Lips ]

246
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:59,015
Yeah, but treat 'em mean,
keep 'em keen. Right, Frank?
Told you before, Murph.

247
00:25:59,098 --> 00:26:02,852
Treat a queen like a whore
and a whore like a queen.

248
00:26:02,935 --> 00:26:05,771
Can't go wrong.

249
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:09,525
What do you think killed Babe?

250
00:26:09,609 --> 00:26:12,194
Beats me. She just keeled over.

251
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:15,865
How old was she?
The charts say 1 1 .

252
00:26:15,949 --> 00:26:19,993
In her prime. Never mind.

253
00:26:20,119 --> 00:26:23,914
We'll chop her up later
and throw her in the stew.
Right.

254
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:28,086
Hey, Frank.

255
00:26:29,087 --> 00:26:31,673
What's this?

256
00:27:17,009 --> 00:27:18,219
[ Clattering ]

257
00:27:33,234 --> 00:27:36,153
"We commit this child...

258
00:27:36,238 --> 00:27:39,824
"and this man
to your keeping, O Lord.

259
00:27:40,826 --> 00:27:43,076
"Their bodies...

260
00:27:43,162 --> 00:27:48,207
"have been taken
from the shadow of our nights.

261
00:27:49,792 --> 00:27:53,755
"They have been released...

262
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:57,967
from all darkness and pain."

263
00:27:58,050 --> 00:28:01,971
[ Gurgling ]

264
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:05,307
"The child and the man...

265
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:09,979
"have gone beyond our world.

266
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:13,857
"They are forever eternal...

267
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:16,152
"and everlasting.

268
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:28,830
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust."

269
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:33,669
[ Dillon ]
Why?

270
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:36,463
Why are the innocent punished?

271
00:28:41,970 --> 00:28:44,971
Why the sacrifice?

272
00:28:47,643 --> 00:28:49,352
Why the pain?

273
00:28:52,189 --> 00:28:55,023
There aren't any promises.

274
00:28:56,317 --> 00:28:59,237
Nothing's certain.

275
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:04,450
Only that some get called,
some get saved.

276
00:29:04,535 --> 00:29:09,329
She won't ever know
the hardship and grief...

277
00:29:09,413 --> 00:29:11,164
for those of us left behind.

278
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:15,795
We commit these bodies
to the void...

279
00:29:15,878 --> 00:29:18,338
with a glad heart.

280
00:29:28,349 --> 00:29:31,269
For within each seed,

281
00:29:31,353 --> 00:29:33,813
there is a promise of a flower.

282
00:29:35,816 --> 00:29:39,861
- [ Gurgling ]
- And within each death,

283
00:29:39,944 --> 00:29:44,198
no matter how small,

284
00:29:44,282 --> 00:29:46,534
there's always a new life.

285
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:53,249
A new beginning.

286
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:56,669
[ Growling ]

287
00:29:56,752 --> 00:29:59,005
Amen.

288
00:30:01,717 --> 00:30:04,218
[ All ]
Amen.

289
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:16,439
[ Squawking ]

290
00:30:33,289 --> 00:30:36,125
[ Man ]
I'll tell you, it's fucking weird.

291
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:38,877
The only one to survive
that crash is a woman.

292
00:30:38,961 --> 00:30:41,087
What trouble can she cause?

293
00:30:41,173 --> 00:30:43,089
She's already changed everything.

294
00:30:43,174 --> 00:30:46,594
[ Chattering Continues ]

295
00:30:46,677 --> 00:30:49,763
[ Water Running ]

296
00:30:52,308 --> 00:30:54,935
What the fuck are we supposed to do-

297
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:58,021
I, for one-
[ Men Chattering, Overlapping ]

298
00:30:59,441 --> 00:31:01,651
I mean it!

299
00:31:11,243 --> 00:31:14,288
[ No Audible Dialogue ]

300
00:31:39,146 --> 00:31:42,232
Okay.

301
00:31:42,317 --> 00:31:47,278
There's a lot of talk going around
that we've got some disharmony here?

302
00:31:47,364 --> 00:31:51,116
Any you guys want to tell me
what the problem is?

303
00:31:51,201 --> 00:31:53,201
[ Sniffs ]

304
00:31:54,496 --> 00:31:56,663
Come on.
Speak to me, brothers.

305
00:31:58,333 --> 00:32:00,500
All right. I'll tell ya.

306
00:32:02,336 --> 00:32:05,047
I don't mind the dark.
I don't mind the bugs.

307
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:09,218
I don't mind wanderin' around in some
cold, wet, damp tunnel for a week at a time.

308
00:32:09,301 --> 00:32:11,971
I don't mind anything.
But I mind Golic.

309
00:32:13,222 --> 00:32:15,307
That the way you feel about it?

310
00:32:15,392 --> 00:32:18,477
Yeah. The guy's crazy
and he smells bad.

311
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:23,148
- [ Snickering ]
-I ain't going out with him anymore.

312
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:29,864
You got anything to say for yourself?

313
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:36,327
Well, he's going with you.

314
00:32:36,413 --> 00:32:41,333
Golic is just another poor, miserable,
suffering son of a bitch, just like you and me.

315
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:43,626
'Cept he smells worse.
And he's crazy.

316
00:32:43,711 --> 00:32:46,172
Knock off the shit!

317
00:32:47,257 --> 00:32:50,300
You got a job to do.

318
00:32:50,384 --> 00:32:54,012
I don't want to hear
another word about Golic.

319
00:32:55,891 --> 00:33:00,853
Okay?

320
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:09,444
[ Chattering ]

321
00:33:17,162 --> 00:33:19,454
[ Man ]
Well, hello.

322
00:33:58,411 --> 00:34:01,830
As I thought, Mr. Aaron.

323
00:34:01,957 --> 00:34:05,125
As I thought.
You called it, sir.

324
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:16,846
I just wanted to, uh, say thanks
for what you said at the funeral.
It was, uh-

325
00:34:18,722 --> 00:34:20,599
My friends would have
appreciated it.

326
00:34:20,684 --> 00:34:23,476
Yeah, well, you don't
wanna know me, lady.

327
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:27,648
I'm a murderer
and rapist of women.

328
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:31,777
Really?

329
00:34:33,405 --> 00:34:37,324
Well, I guess
I must make you nervous.

330
00:34:52,715 --> 00:34:56,427
- Do you have any faith, sister?
- Not much.

331
00:34:56,510 --> 00:35:01,389
Well, we've got a lot of faith here.
Enough even for you.

332
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:04,101
I thought women weren't allowed.

333
00:35:04,186 --> 00:35:06,103
Well, we've never had any before,

334
00:35:06,188 --> 00:35:10,440
but we tolerate anybody.

335
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:15,153
- Even the intolerable.
- Thank you.

336
00:35:15,237 --> 00:35:19,909
That's just a statement of principle.
Nothing personal.

337
00:35:19,992 --> 00:35:23,329
You see, we've got
a good place to wait here.

338
00:35:23,413 --> 00:35:27,041
And until now, no temptation.

339
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:35,507
What are you waiting for?

340
00:35:39,971 --> 00:35:43,056
Huh!
[ Chuckles ]

341
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:47,518
We're waiting for God to return...

342
00:35:47,603 --> 00:35:51,440
and raise his servants to redemption.

343
00:35:53,525 --> 00:35:58,530
[ Clemens ]
Dillon and the rest
of the alternative people...

344
00:35:58,614 --> 00:36:03,159
embraced religion, as it were,
about five years ago.

345
00:36:03,286 --> 00:36:06,371
Tincture?
[ Ripley ]
I'm on medication.

346
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,958
Hardly.
What kind of religion?

347
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:14,463
Some sort of apocalyptic, millenarian,
Christian fundamentalist, uh-

348
00:36:14,588 --> 00:36:16,923
Right.
Exactly.

349
00:36:17,007 --> 00:36:19,842
Point is, when the company
wanted to close the facility down,

350
00:36:19,927 --> 00:36:23,597
Dillon and the rest of the converts
wanted to stay.

351
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:27,809
And they were allowed
to remain as custodians...

352
00:36:27,893 --> 00:36:30,813
with two minders...

353
00:36:30,896 --> 00:36:33,565
and a medical officer.

354
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:35,733
And here we are.

355
00:36:35,818 --> 00:36:38,112
How did you get
this wonderful assignment?

356
00:36:41,407 --> 00:36:43,324
How do you like
your new haircut?

357
00:36:45,244 --> 00:36:47,161
It's okay.

358
00:37:04,264 --> 00:37:07,974
Now that I've gone out on a limb
for you with Andrews,

359
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:11,311
damaged my already less-than-perfect
relationship with that good man,

360
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:13,813
and briefed you...

361
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:17,735
on the humdrum history
of Fury 1 61 ,

362
00:37:17,818 --> 00:37:20,195
can you not tell me
what you were looking for in the girl?

363
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:23,324
You attracted to me?

364
00:37:23,407 --> 00:37:25,492
ln what way?

365
00:37:27,661 --> 00:37:29,663
ln that way.

366
00:37:31,458 --> 00:37:34,001
Very direct.

367
00:37:35,045 --> 00:37:37,378
I've been out here a long time.

368
00:37:40,050 --> 00:37:41,967
So have I.

369
00:37:46,181 --> 00:37:51,601
♪ In the year 751 0 ♪

370
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:53,853
♪ If God's a-comin' ♪

371
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:57,608
♪ He oughta make it by then ♪

372
00:37:57,692 --> 00:38:01,277
♪ Maybe he'll look around and say ♪

373
00:38:01,362 --> 00:38:04,655
♪ Guess it's time for the Judgment- ♪

374
00:38:28,556 --> 00:38:30,264
Yech!

375
00:38:32,559 --> 00:38:34,561
♪ In the year ♪♪

376
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:44,570
Hey, Spike.
Spike? Spikey!

377
00:38:49,827 --> 00:38:52,954
Are you down there?
What are you doing?

378
00:39:00,045 --> 00:39:03,257
[ Screaming , Indistinct ]

379
00:39:37,458 --> 00:39:40,043
I really appreciate your affections,

380
00:39:41,963 --> 00:39:44,965
but I am aware that they...
deflected my question.

381
00:39:46,925 --> 00:39:49,887
In the nicest possible way, of course.

382
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:55,809
[ Ripley ]
You're spoiling the mood.

383
00:39:56,811 --> 00:39:59,730
I have a job to do.
[ Clears Throat ]

384
00:39:59,813 --> 00:40:02,190
I just want to know why
we had to cremate the bodies.

385
00:40:02,275 --> 00:40:05,652
And now that I'm in your cot,

386
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:08,112
you think I owe you an answer.

387
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:10,907
I think you owe me an answer.

388
00:40:10,992 --> 00:40:13,202
Being in my bed's
got nothing to do with it.

389
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:16,204
[ Sighs ]

390
00:40:17,623 --> 00:40:21,543
I had a terrible dream in hypersleep.

391
00:40:21,628 --> 00:40:24,378
And I had to be sure what killed her.

392
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:26,715
Anyway, I made a mistake.

393
00:40:26,798 --> 00:40:29,592
Possibly.

394
00:40:29,677 --> 00:40:33,722
[ Sighs ]
And now I've made
another mistake.

395
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,724
Really? What's that?

396
00:40:35,807 --> 00:40:38,434
Fraternizing with a prisoner.

397
00:40:38,519 --> 00:40:42,688
Physical contact.
It's against the rules, isn't it?

398
00:40:42,773 --> 00:40:46,902
Definitely. When was this?

399
00:40:46,985 --> 00:40:49,570
l think you know.

400
00:40:54,869 --> 00:40:56,911
I'm not a prisoner.

401
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:02,041
You have a bar code
on the back of your head.

402
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:06,295
[ Sighs ]

403
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:09,007
That does deserve an explanation.

404
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:14,012
But I don't think
now is the moment.

405
00:41:16,056 --> 00:41:20,226
Sorry. We are rather
spoiling things, aren't we?

406
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:24,438
[ Intercom Buzzes ]
[ Assistant On Intercom ]
Mr. Clemens.

407
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:29,652
Mr. Aaron.
Superintendent Andrews
would like you to report...

408
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:33,447
to vent shaft 22
on the second quadrant- now.

409
00:41:33,574 --> 00:41:35,617
We've had an accident.
Something serious?

410
00:41:35,702 --> 00:41:41,039
You could call it that.
One of our prisoners has been... diced.

411
00:41:41,123 --> 00:41:44,876
Sorry. I have to go.

412
00:41:47,255 --> 00:41:49,255
Official duties.

413
00:41:50,757 --> 00:41:53,260
[ Door Opens ]

414
00:41:56,681 --> 00:41:58,681
[ Door Closes ]

415
00:42:17,577 --> 00:42:21,121
- Who was it?
- Murphy.

416
00:42:21,204 --> 00:42:23,206
How do you know?

417
00:42:23,291 --> 00:42:25,791
That's his boot.

418
00:42:27,461 --> 00:42:30,255
I gave him the assignment, sir.
He was a wanker.

419
00:42:30,340 --> 00:42:32,757
No apologies, Mr. Aaron.
It wasn't your fault.

420
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:46,730
Well, not much to say, is there?

421
00:42:46,813 --> 00:42:49,858
Death was instantaneous.
No shit.

422
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:52,318
I take it he was pulled
into the fan.

423
00:42:52,402 --> 00:42:54,362
Sudden rush of air,
I'd imagine, except-

424
00:42:54,447 --> 00:42:56,530
Right.
Almost happened to me once.

425
00:42:56,615 --> 00:43:00,994
I've told him so many times,
"Stay away from the fans."

426
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:02,996
Nobody bloody listens.

427
00:43:03,081 --> 00:43:06,208
Except the fan was blowing.

428
00:43:13,173 --> 00:43:15,257
- What's that?
- I don't know.

429
00:43:15,342 --> 00:43:20,137
I want to see you in my quarters
in 30 minutes, if you'll please, Mr. Clemens.

430
00:43:25,644 --> 00:43:28,521
[ Aaron ]
Have you got any ideas?

431
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:58,760
[ Gas Hissing ]

432
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:07,184
[ Beeping ]

433
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:17,153
Here you are. You know,
wandering around without an escort...

434
00:44:17,237 --> 00:44:21,074
is really gonna piss
Superintendent Andrews off.

435
00:44:21,159 --> 00:44:23,492
Will you tell me
about your accident?

436
00:44:23,577 --> 00:44:27,204
One of the prisoners has been killed.

437
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:29,666
Really? How?
Hmm.

438
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:32,293
In the air shaft.

439
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:34,880
Poor soul backed into a nine-foot fan.

440
00:44:36,047 --> 00:44:38,382
I found something
at the accident site,

441
00:44:38,467 --> 00:44:41,887
just a bit away
from where it happened.

442
00:44:41,971 --> 00:44:45,556
A mark. A burn.

443
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:49,936
Rather like the one you found
on the girl's cryo-tube.

444
00:44:56,318 --> 00:45:00,237
Look. I'm on your side.

445
00:45:00,322 --> 00:45:03,824
I want to help, but I need to know
what's going on...

446
00:45:03,909 --> 00:45:06,286
or what you think is going on.

447
00:45:08,914 --> 00:45:10,916
lf you really wanna help,

448
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:13,168
find me a computer
with audio capabilities...

449
00:45:13,251 --> 00:45:15,378
so I can access this flight recorder.

450
00:45:15,463 --> 00:45:17,588
We don't have anything
like that here.

451
00:45:17,715 --> 00:45:19,882
[ Sighs ]
Well, what about Bishop?
Bishop?

452
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:22,469
The droid that crashed with me.

453
00:45:22,552 --> 00:45:24,929
I can point you in the right direction.

454
00:45:25,014 --> 00:45:27,014
I can't join you.

455
00:45:27,099 --> 00:45:30,309
I have a previous engagement.

456
00:45:31,896 --> 00:45:35,731
This'll top you up.
Golic, don't fidget.

457
00:45:35,815 --> 00:45:40,695
What's all this shit?
It's not properly wrapped.

458
00:45:40,820 --> 00:45:42,905
What the hell
does he ever do right?
Eat.

459
00:45:43,032 --> 00:45:45,324
He's got that down pretty good.
Golic!

460
00:45:45,409 --> 00:45:49,496
You light a candle for Murphy.
I'll light a thousand.

461
00:45:51,958 --> 00:45:54,501
[ Golic ]
He was special.

462
00:45:54,585 --> 00:45:57,878
Never complained
about me once.

463
00:45:57,963 --> 00:46:00,005
I loved him.

464
00:46:02,927 --> 00:46:05,929
Is it true what they say?

465
00:46:06,012 --> 00:46:08,347
His head split into a million pieces?

466
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:11,184
[ Man ]
Okay. Who's got the matches?
[ Door Slams ]

467
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:18,023
- Sit down, Mr. Clemens.
- Thank you.

468
00:46:20,860 --> 00:46:22,820
Sugar?
Uh, no thanks.

469
00:46:22,947 --> 00:46:25,447
Milk?
Just a little, please.

470
00:46:29,202 --> 00:46:31,246
Thank you, Mr. Aaron.

471
00:46:41,007 --> 00:46:43,257
Listen to me, you piece of shit.

472
00:46:43,342 --> 00:46:46,219
You screw with me
one more time, I'll cut you in half.

473
00:46:47,471 --> 00:46:49,514
I'm sorry.
I don't think I understand.

474
00:46:49,599 --> 00:46:52,641
At 0700 hours, I received word
from the network.

475
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:55,561
I may point out this is the first
high-level communication...

476
00:46:55,646 --> 00:46:59,773
this installation has ever received,
to my knowledge.

477
00:46:59,858 --> 00:47:01,735
They want this woman looked after.

478
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:04,570
They consider her to be
very high priority.
Why?

479
00:47:04,655 --> 00:47:06,947
l have no idea.

480
00:47:07,032 --> 00:47:10,327
But why did you let her
out of the infirmary?

481
00:47:10,411 --> 00:47:12,579
This accident with Murphy
is what happens...

482
00:47:12,663 --> 00:47:15,664
when one of these dumb sons of a bitches
walks around with a hard-on.

483
00:47:15,750 --> 00:47:18,460
I'm a doctor. You're the jailer.

484
00:47:20,211 --> 00:47:23,840
We both know exactly what you are.

485
00:47:23,965 --> 00:47:27,092
Sit down.
I think it might be better if I left.

486
00:47:27,177 --> 00:47:30,889
I find you...
unpleasant to be around.

487
00:47:30,972 --> 00:47:34,351
You do? Isn't that lovely?
Consider this, Mr. Clemens.

488
00:47:34,434 --> 00:47:37,519
How would you like me to explain
your sordid history...

489
00:47:37,605 --> 00:47:39,856
to your newfound friend?

490
00:47:39,940 --> 00:47:43,735
For her personal
edification, of course.

491
00:47:43,818 --> 00:47:46,445
Now sit the hell down.

492
00:47:56,998 --> 00:48:00,168
I don't like you.
You're unpredictable.

493
00:48:00,251 --> 00:48:03,045
Insolent. Possibly dangerous.

494
00:48:03,130 --> 00:48:06,007
You question everything!

495
00:48:06,092 --> 00:48:08,550
If I didn't need a medical officer,

496
00:48:08,635 --> 00:48:10,887
I wouldn't let you within
light years of this operation.

497
00:48:10,971 --> 00:48:14,181
- I'm eternally grateful.
- Keep your sarcasms to yourself.

498
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:18,268
Now, is there anything I should know?

499
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:22,106
About what?
About the woman.

500
00:48:22,190 --> 00:48:25,735
Don't play with me, Mr. Clemens.
You spend every second you can with her.

501
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:29,322
And I have my suspicions not all of
your concerns with her are medical.

502
00:48:33,702 --> 00:48:38,581
Has she said anything to you- anything
about where she's from, what her mission is?

503
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:40,833
What the hell she was doing in an E.E.V.?

504
00:48:40,918 --> 00:48:43,711
She told me she was part of a combat unit
that came to grief.

505
00:48:43,795 --> 00:48:46,297
Beyond that, I assume it's all classified.

506
00:48:46,382 --> 00:48:49,717
I haven't pressed her for more.

507
00:48:49,802 --> 00:48:51,802
That's all?
That's all.

508
00:48:51,929 --> 00:48:53,972
You're sure?
Yes.

509
00:48:54,097 --> 00:48:57,182
Nothing more?
No.

510
00:49:00,855 --> 00:49:02,896
Get out of here.

511
00:49:12,699 --> 00:49:15,201
[ Door Closes ]

512
00:49:19,039 --> 00:49:21,875
[ Thunderclap ]

513
00:49:53,072 --> 00:49:55,365
[ Grunts ]

514
00:50:02,081 --> 00:50:04,501
[ Thunderclap ]

515
00:50:48,628 --> 00:50:51,588
[ Grunting ]

516
00:50:51,673 --> 00:50:54,050
- [ Screams ]
- Shut up, you fuckin' bitch!

517
00:50:54,134 --> 00:50:56,510
- Get in there!
- Shut up, you bitch!

518
00:50:56,594 --> 00:51:00,764
- Nobody's gonna hear you.
- Goddamn it, let go of me!

519
00:51:00,849 --> 00:51:03,434
Fuck you! No!

520
00:51:03,561 --> 00:51:06,563
Hold still! Shh! Shh!
[ Shouting ]

521
00:51:06,646 --> 00:51:08,398
No! Goddamn it!

522
00:51:08,481 --> 00:51:12,318
[ Roars ]

523
00:51:13,862 --> 00:51:16,197
[ Grunts, Groans ]

524
00:51:16,282 --> 00:51:18,324
You okay?

525
00:51:19,492 --> 00:51:22,619
No! Son of a bitch!

526
00:51:28,168 --> 00:51:32,380
Take off. I gotta reeducate
some of the brothers.

527
00:51:32,463 --> 00:51:35,300
We've gotta discuss
some matters of the spirit.

528
00:51:41,514 --> 00:51:43,516
[ Groans ]

529
00:51:46,811 --> 00:51:48,813
Cigarettes!

530
00:52:05,748 --> 00:52:07,748
So let's do it.

531
00:52:13,547 --> 00:52:16,590
[ Man ]
This is like 1 0 city blocks.

532
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:19,052
[ Man Chewing Loudly ]

533
00:52:19,177 --> 00:52:25,099
How many?
This makes 1 76.

534
00:52:25,184 --> 00:52:27,768
Can't you chew a little quieter?

535
00:52:27,853 --> 00:52:30,021
I'm trying to figure out
how big this compartment is.

536
00:52:30,105 --> 00:52:32,898
I can't think with all this
goddamn noise you're making.

537
00:52:33,025 --> 00:52:35,860
You're not supposed to swear.
I'm sorry.

538
00:52:35,945 --> 00:52:40,364
- Now, we've encircled
this entire compartment once-
- Hey.

539
00:52:40,449 --> 00:52:42,909
What?

540
00:52:46,871 --> 00:52:48,831
What the shit is doing that?

541
00:52:48,916 --> 00:52:50,666
Swearing.
Shut up.

542
00:52:50,751 --> 00:52:53,251
It's all right to say "shit."
It ain't against God.

543
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:55,713
What the hell is going on
with the candles?

544
00:53:00,177 --> 00:53:03,012
Must be the wind
from one of the vent shafts.

545
00:53:03,097 --> 00:53:05,889
Backwash from the closest
circulating unit.

546
00:53:05,974 --> 00:53:08,976
But if all the candles go out,
how the hell we gonna know
where we are?

547
00:53:09,061 --> 00:53:12,355
Somebody will just have to
go back and relight them.

548
00:53:12,438 --> 00:53:15,233
I guess I'm nominated.

549
00:53:24,909 --> 00:53:27,577
Watch your step, brother.

550
00:53:36,672 --> 00:53:40,465
Okay, who are the comedians?

551
00:54:02,322 --> 00:54:04,322
[ Liquid Dripping ]

552
00:54:14,333 --> 00:54:16,168
[ Screeches ]

553
00:54:18,338 --> 00:54:20,922
[ Man Screaming ]

554
00:54:23,469 --> 00:54:26,429
[ Both Screaming ]

555
00:54:26,512 --> 00:54:28,431
Wait, wait, wait!

556
00:54:28,514 --> 00:54:30,682
- Quick, grab it. Here.
- Help me! Help me!

557
00:54:32,478 --> 00:54:35,521
Go! Fuckin' go!

558
00:54:37,440 --> 00:54:40,902
Go, go, go! Quick! Run!

559
00:54:42,362 --> 00:54:44,864
[ Both Screaming ]

560
00:54:50,119 --> 00:54:52,121
Gimme that!

561
00:55:26,155 --> 00:55:28,574
[ No Audible Dialogue ]

562
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:30,201
[ Clattering ]

563
00:55:32,036 --> 00:55:34,454
[ Screams ]
Get this fucking thing off me!

564
00:55:34,539 --> 00:55:36,748
Oh, fuck!

565
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:38,793
Let me go!
[ Screams ]

566
00:55:39,753 --> 00:55:41,753
[ Screams ]

567
00:55:48,427 --> 00:55:50,637
[ Screaming ]

568
00:55:52,891 --> 00:55:55,059
[ Beeping ]

569
00:56:29,510 --> 00:56:31,637
[ Beeping Continues ]

570
00:56:32,681 --> 00:56:34,681
[ Servo Whirs ]

571
00:56:36,893 --> 00:56:38,894
[ Softly ]
Hey.

572
00:56:40,271 --> 00:56:42,481
Ah, Ripley.

573
00:56:42,565 --> 00:56:46,193
Hi, Bishop.
How you feeling?

574
00:56:46,277 --> 00:56:48,237
My legs hurt.

575
00:56:48,322 --> 00:56:50,530
Uh, listen, I'm sorry.

576
00:56:50,615 --> 00:56:53,201
It's okay.
I'm just a glorified toaster.

577
00:56:53,284 --> 00:56:55,286
How are you?

578
00:56:56,621 --> 00:56:58,914
I like your new haircut.

579
00:56:58,998 --> 00:57:01,250
Bishop, can you access data
on the flight recorder?

580
00:57:01,335 --> 00:57:02,001
No problem.

581
00:57:04,838 --> 00:57:06,463
[ Beeping ]

582
00:57:06,547 --> 00:57:10,175
[ Spoon Clanging ]
[ Slurping ]

583
00:57:28,987 --> 00:57:31,322
Golic?

584
00:57:36,077 --> 00:57:39,329
I'm home.
What happened on the Sulaco?

585
00:57:39,414 --> 00:57:42,041
Why were our cryo-tubes ejected?

586
00:57:42,125 --> 00:57:44,668
[ Computer Voice ]
Stasis interrupted.

587
00:57:44,753 --> 00:57:48,630
Fire in cryogenic compartment.

588
00:57:48,757 --> 00:57:52,217
Repeat. Fire in cryogenic-
What happened?

589
00:57:52,302 --> 00:57:54,844
What started the fire, Bishop?

590
00:57:54,929 --> 00:57:56,931
Can you hear me?

591
00:57:58,224 --> 00:58:00,226
[ Normal Voice ]
The fire was electrical.

592
00:58:00,309 --> 00:58:03,561
lt was in the subflooring.

593
00:58:03,646 --> 00:58:07,233
Did the sensors pick up anything
moving around on the ship prior to separation?

594
00:58:07,317 --> 00:58:10,777
It's very dark here, Ripley.
I'm not what I used to be.

595
00:58:10,862 --> 00:58:15,240
Just tell me. Does the recorder
indicate anything?

596
00:58:15,324 --> 00:58:17,784
Was there an alien on board?

597
00:58:19,286 --> 00:58:21,079
Yes.

598
00:58:24,418 --> 00:58:28,545
Is it on the Sulaco or did it
come with us on the E.E.V.?

599
00:58:28,630 --> 00:58:31,923
It was with us all the way.

600
00:58:34,344 --> 00:58:36,262
[ Slurping ]

601
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:50,233
Does the company know?

602
00:58:50,318 --> 00:58:53,528
The company knows everything
that happened on the ship.

603
00:58:53,612 --> 00:58:57,992
It all goes into the computer
and gets sent back to network.

604
00:58:58,076 --> 00:59:00,036
And they want it.

605
00:59:00,119 --> 00:59:05,416
I hurt. Do me a favor.
Disconnect me.

606
00:59:05,500 --> 00:59:09,586
I could be reworked,
but I'll never be top of the line again.

607
00:59:09,670 --> 00:59:12,338
I'd rather be nothing.

608
00:59:12,423 --> 00:59:14,925
You're sure?

609
00:59:16,677 --> 00:59:19,304
Do it for me, Ripley.

610
00:59:24,978 --> 00:59:26,896
[ Whirring ]

611
00:59:26,980 --> 00:59:28,981
[ Exhales ]

612
00:59:31,275 --> 00:59:31,983
[ Men Chattering ]

613
00:59:33,402 --> 00:59:37,322
It wasn't me! I didn't do it!

614
00:59:37,407 --> 00:59:41,534
[ Chattering ]
It was- It was the dragon.

615
00:59:41,619 --> 00:59:43,788
Feeds on minds. It was-

616
00:59:43,914 --> 00:59:46,248
Nobody can stop it.
What about Boggs and Rains?

617
00:59:46,333 --> 00:59:48,666
They got s-slaughtered like pigs.
It wasn't me!

618
00:59:48,751 --> 00:59:53,505
- It wasn't me!
- Stark raving mad.

619
00:59:53,590 --> 00:59:56,257
I'm not saying it was anyone's fault,
but he should have been chained up.

620
00:59:56,342 --> 00:59:59,677
You called it, sir.
Mad as a fucking hatter.

621
00:59:59,762 --> 01:00:03,556
Keep him separated from the rest.
I don't want him causing a panic.

622
01:00:03,641 --> 01:00:05,809
Clemens,
sedate this poor idiot.
Yeah?

623
01:00:05,893 --> 01:00:08,311
Not until we know about the brothers.

624
01:00:08,396 --> 01:00:12,233
Now, now. Pull yourself together.
Talk to me now.

625
01:00:12,358 --> 01:00:15,235
Now, where are Boggs and Rains?
It wasn't me!

626
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:17,195
[ Andrews ]
Hopeless. You're not gonna
get anything out of him.

627
01:00:17,322 --> 01:00:20,157
It wasn't me.
We'll have to send out
a search team.

628
01:00:20,242 --> 01:00:22,576
I'm afraid we'll have to assume
there's a very good chance...

629
01:00:22,661 --> 01:00:24,994
this simple bastard
has murdered them.

630
01:00:26,873 --> 01:00:29,250
Now, you don't know that.

631
01:00:30,251 --> 01:00:33,003
He's never lied to me.

632
01:00:33,088 --> 01:00:36,340
He's crazy, he's a fool,
but he's not a liar.

633
01:00:38,385 --> 01:00:40,719
He's telling the truth.

634
01:00:40,804 --> 01:00:43,931
I'd like to talk to him
about this- this dragon.

635
01:00:44,014 --> 01:00:46,976
- It was a dragon.
- [ Andrews ] You're not talking
to anyone, Lieutenant.

636
01:00:47,059 --> 01:00:49,936
I'm not interested in your opinion,

637
01:00:50,021 --> 01:00:52,148
because you are not
in full possession of the facts.

638
01:00:52,231 --> 01:00:55,775
This man is a convicted multiple murderer,
known for particularly brutal crimes.

639
01:00:55,860 --> 01:00:58,528
Isn't that right, Mr. Dillon?

640
01:00:58,612 --> 01:01:01,407
Yeah. That part's right.

641
01:01:03,827 --> 01:01:06,327
Then I'll talk to you. lt's important.

642
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:08,831
When I have finished
with my official duties,

643
01:01:08,914 --> 01:01:12,041
I will be quite pleased
to have a little chat, yes?

644
01:01:16,422 --> 01:01:21,802
Let me see if I have
this correct, Lieutenant.
It's an eight-foot creature of some kind,

645
01:01:21,887 --> 01:01:26,139
with acid for blood,
and it arrived on your spaceship.

646
01:01:26,224 --> 01:01:29,726
It kills on sight
and is generally unpleasant.

647
01:01:29,811 --> 01:01:32,353
And, of course, you expect me to accept
all this on your word.

648
01:01:32,438 --> 01:01:34,815
No, I don't expect anything.

649
01:01:34,900 --> 01:01:39,737
- Quite a story, Mr. Aaron.
- Right, sir. It's a beauty.

650
01:01:39,820 --> 01:01:42,780
- Never heard anything quite like it, sir.
- Expect not.

651
01:01:42,865 --> 01:01:44,949
Tell me, Lieutenant,
what would you suggest we do?

652
01:01:47,329 --> 01:01:49,746
Well, what kind
of weapons have you got?

653
01:01:49,831 --> 01:01:51,831
This is a prison.

654
01:01:51,916 --> 01:01:54,376
It's not a good idea to allow prisoners
access to firearms.

655
01:01:54,460 --> 01:01:56,253
What keeps them from killing you?

656
01:01:56,338 --> 01:01:59,297
Fear. There's no way to escape.

657
01:01:59,382 --> 01:02:03,344
With the arrival of the next supply ship,
the company would eliminate them.

658
01:02:03,427 --> 01:02:07,306
This is a maximum security prison,

659
01:02:08,807 --> 01:02:12,518
and you have no weapons of any kind?

660
01:02:14,813 --> 01:02:18,608
We have some carving knives in the abattoir.
A few more in the mess hall.

661
01:02:18,693 --> 01:02:22,112
Some fire axes scattered about the place.
Nothing terribly formidable.

662
01:02:22,197 --> 01:02:23,489
That's all?

663
01:02:23,572 --> 01:02:25,324
We're on the honor system.

664
01:02:31,331 --> 01:02:35,541
- Then we're fucked.
- No, you're fucked.

665
01:02:35,626 --> 01:02:39,003
Confined to the infirmary.
Quarantined.

666
01:02:39,088 --> 01:02:41,798
Mr. Aaron will escort you.

667
01:02:41,882 --> 01:02:46,177
I think you'll be safe from any large,
nasty beast while you're there, right?

668
01:02:48,181 --> 01:02:51,349
Yes, that's a good girl.

669
01:02:54,353 --> 01:02:58,023
[ Intercom Buzzes ]
[ Aaron ]
Let's all report to the mess hall.

670
01:02:58,108 --> 01:03:02,110
Superintendent Andrews wants a meeting.
Mess hall, right away, people.

671
01:03:02,195 --> 01:03:06,282
Isn't there any way off of this place?
Some way to escape?

672
01:03:06,365 --> 01:03:10,119
[ Laughs ]
No. Supply ship comes every six months.

673
01:03:10,202 --> 01:03:12,204
And that's it?
Mm-hmm.

674
01:03:12,289 --> 01:03:15,123
Fuck.

675
01:03:15,208 --> 01:03:19,460
They are sending somebody
to pick you up quite soon, I gather.

676
01:03:19,545 --> 01:03:22,338
Really.
[ Coughs ]
What's "soon"?

677
01:03:22,423 --> 01:03:27,094
I don't know. Nobody's ever been
in a hurry to get here before.

678
01:03:29,764 --> 01:03:32,682
Do you want to tell me
what you and Andrews talked about?

679
01:03:32,766 --> 01:03:35,018
No.

680
01:03:35,144 --> 01:03:39,148
You'll just say I'm crazy.
[ Liquid Swishing ]

681
01:03:39,231 --> 01:03:45,195
- That's a bit uncharitable.
- [ Inhales, Coughing ]

682
01:03:48,365 --> 01:03:50,326
How are you feeling?

683
01:03:50,409 --> 01:03:54,538
[ Sighs ]
Not so hot.
[ Clears Throat ]

684
01:03:54,621 --> 01:03:56,539
Sore throat.

685
01:03:56,623 --> 01:04:00,543
Sick to my stomach.
Pissed off.

686
01:04:00,628 --> 01:04:04,505
Well, that's understandable
given the circumstances.

687
01:04:04,590 --> 01:04:08,052
Perhaps I should give you
one of my special cocktails.

688
01:04:08,177 --> 01:04:10,971
[ Golic ]
I don't know why everybody
blames everybody for everything.

689
01:04:11,056 --> 01:04:13,474
Nobody's persect, only human.

690
01:04:15,684 --> 01:04:17,978
There's no such thing
as a perfect human.

691
01:04:18,063 --> 01:04:21,148
In an insane world,

692
01:04:21,231 --> 01:04:23,692
a sane man...

693
01:04:23,777 --> 01:04:28,237
must... appear... insane.

694
01:04:28,322 --> 01:04:31,909
That's very profound, Golic.
Thank you.

695
01:04:37,664 --> 01:04:40,541
You married?

696
01:04:40,626 --> 01:04:43,211
Me?
You should get married,
have kids.

697
01:04:43,295 --> 01:04:48,509
Pretty girl. I used to know
lots of 'em back home.

698
01:04:48,592 --> 01:04:51,469
They used to like me.

699
01:04:53,931 --> 01:04:55,932
For a while.

700
01:05:00,980 --> 01:05:02,940
You're gonna die too.

701
01:05:10,989 --> 01:05:14,701
Are you?
What?

702
01:05:14,786 --> 01:05:17,036
Married.

703
01:05:17,121 --> 01:05:19,539
[ Ripley ]
Why?

704
01:05:19,623 --> 01:05:22,876
- Just curious.
- No.

705
01:05:25,797 --> 01:05:31,050
- How about leveling with me?
- Could you be more specific?

706
01:05:31,135 --> 01:05:34,762
When I asked how you got assigned here,
you avoided the question.

707
01:05:34,847 --> 01:05:38,057
And then when I asked about the prison I.D.
tattooed on the back of your head,

708
01:05:38,143 --> 01:05:40,018
you ducked me again.

709
01:05:42,981 --> 01:05:45,190
lt's a long, sad story...

710
01:05:46,400 --> 01:05:48,735
and more than
a little melodramatic.

711
01:05:48,820 --> 01:05:51,195
Try me.

712
01:05:53,199 --> 01:05:55,701
[ Liquid Swishing ]
If you insist.

713
01:06:00,414 --> 01:06:02,748
After my student years,

714
01:06:03,876 --> 01:06:06,836
despite the fact that I had become...

715
01:06:06,920 --> 01:06:09,338
secretly addicted to morphine,

716
01:06:09,423 --> 01:06:11,675
I was considered
to be most promising,

717
01:06:11,759 --> 01:06:14,219
a man with a future.

718
01:06:17,222 --> 01:06:21,518
And during my first residency,
I did a 36-hour stretch on an E.R.

719
01:06:22,769 --> 01:06:26,315
So, I went out and I got
more than a little drunk.

720
01:06:26,398 --> 01:06:28,567
Then I got called back.

721
01:06:28,650 --> 01:06:30,818
Boiler had blown on a fuel plant,

722
01:06:30,903 --> 01:06:33,989
and there were 30 casualties.

723
01:06:34,072 --> 01:06:36,407
And 1 1 of them died.

724
01:06:36,492 --> 01:06:38,659
Not as a result of the accident...

725
01:06:38,744 --> 01:06:41,204
but because I prescribed
the wrong dosage of painkiller.

726
01:06:43,333 --> 01:06:47,335
I got seven years in prison
and my license reduced to a 3-C.

727
01:06:50,297 --> 01:06:52,632
At least I got off the morphine.

728
01:06:52,717 --> 01:06:54,885
l'm sorry.

729
01:06:56,637 --> 01:06:58,804
l think I was let off lightly.

730
01:06:58,889 --> 01:07:01,807
Did you serve your time here?

731
01:07:03,978 --> 01:07:06,896
I got to know
this motley crew quite well.

732
01:07:06,981 --> 01:07:10,858
So when they stayed, I stayed.

733
01:07:12,277 --> 01:07:14,612
Nobody else would employ me.

734
01:07:18,034 --> 01:07:21,786
So, do you still trust me
with a needle?

735
01:07:45,936 --> 01:07:48,146
[ Whimpering ]

736
01:08:02,202 --> 01:08:04,788
[ Hisses, Screeches ]

737
01:08:07,750 --> 01:08:08,875
[ Whimpering ]

738
01:08:27,185 --> 01:08:29,186
[ Growls, Hisses ]
[ Yelps ]

739
01:08:35,403 --> 01:08:37,404
[ Whimpering ]

740
01:08:50,792 --> 01:08:53,377
Magnificent.

741
01:08:57,716 --> 01:09:00,426
[ Dillon ]
Give us strength, O Lord, to endure.

742
01:09:00,511 --> 01:09:05,056
We recognize that we are poor sinners
in the hands of an angry God.

743
01:09:05,140 --> 01:09:09,478
Let the circle be unbroken
until the day. Amen.

744
01:09:09,604 --> 01:09:13,064
[ All ] Amen.
[ Dillon ]
What the fuck is happening here?

745
01:09:14,484 --> 01:09:17,903
What the fuck is this
bullshit that's comin' down?

746
01:09:17,987 --> 01:09:20,988
We got murder. We got rape.
We got brothers in trouble.

747
01:09:21,073 --> 01:09:25,452
I don't want no more bullshit
around here!

748
01:09:25,536 --> 01:09:30,247
Now, we got problems,
we stand together.

749
01:09:30,332 --> 01:09:33,167
Yes. Thank you, Mr. Dillon. All right.

750
01:09:33,252 --> 01:09:36,380
Once again, this is rumor control.

751
01:09:36,463 --> 01:09:39,006
Here are the facts.

752
01:09:39,091 --> 01:09:41,760
At 0800 hours,
prisoner Murphy,

753
01:09:41,844 --> 01:09:44,680
through carelessness on his part,

754
01:09:44,764 --> 01:09:47,599
was found dead in vent shaft 1 7.

755
01:09:47,684 --> 01:09:50,226
He seems to have been
sucked into a ventilator fan.

756
01:09:51,604 --> 01:09:53,604
[ Gasping ]

757
01:09:53,689 --> 01:09:56,440
At about 21 00 hours,

758
01:09:56,525 --> 01:10:00,654
prisoner Golic reappeared
in a deranged state.

759
01:10:00,738 --> 01:10:03,030
Prisoners Boggs and Rains are missing.

760
01:10:03,115 --> 01:10:07,786
There seems to be a good chance
that they have met with foul play...

761
01:10:07,869 --> 01:10:11,122
at the hands of prisoner Golic.
[ Mutters ]

762
01:10:13,083 --> 01:10:15,918
We need to organize
and send out a search party.

763
01:10:17,755 --> 01:10:20,631
Volunteers will be appreciated.

764
01:10:23,219 --> 01:10:27,389
I think it's fair to say
that our smoothly running facility...

765
01:10:27,472 --> 01:10:30,307
has suddenly developed
a few problems.

766
01:10:30,393 --> 01:10:36,273
I can only hope we are able to all
pull together over the next few days...

767
01:10:36,356 --> 01:10:39,568
until the rescue team arrives
for Lieutenant Ripley.

768
01:10:39,652 --> 01:10:41,610
lt's here! It got Clemens!

769
01:10:41,695 --> 01:10:45,407
- Stop this raving at once! Stop it!
- I'm telling you, it's here!

770
01:10:45,490 --> 01:10:48,409
Aaron, get that foolish woman
back to the infirmary!

771
01:10:48,493 --> 01:10:51,621
- [ Screams ]
- [ All Shouting ]

772
01:10:51,706 --> 01:10:53,664
[ Man ]
Move it!

773
01:10:55,083 --> 01:10:56,333
Out of my way!

774
01:10:59,963 --> 01:11:01,965
Fuck!

775
01:11:08,722 --> 01:11:11,765
[ Dillon ]
We give you thanks, O Lord.

776
01:11:11,850 --> 01:11:16,854
Your wrath has come,
and the time is near for us to be judged.

777
01:11:17,899 --> 01:11:21,902
The apocalypse is upon us.

778
01:11:21,985 --> 01:11:27,615
Let us be ready.
Let your mercy be just.

779
01:11:27,699 --> 01:11:29,326
It was massive.
Amen!

780
01:11:29,452 --> 01:11:31,994
And fast.
l was there. I saw it.

781
01:11:32,078 --> 01:11:36,416
What the fuck do we do now?
Who's in fucking charge?

782
01:11:40,421 --> 01:11:42,922
[ Man ]
Organize. We gotta organize, right?

783
01:11:43,006 --> 01:11:45,716
Right. Well, I guess
I'm next in line.

784
01:11:45,801 --> 01:11:49,386
- 85's gonna be in charge.
Jesus, give us a break!
- Don't call me that.

785
01:11:49,471 --> 01:11:51,847
[ Aaron ]
Okay, look. There's no way
I can replace Andrews.

786
01:11:51,932 --> 01:11:54,643
He was a good man.
I know you guys didn't appreciate him.

787
01:11:54,726 --> 01:11:57,895
Aaron, we don't want
to hear that shit now.

788
01:11:57,979 --> 01:12:01,024
Hey, sister, what about you?
You're an officer.

789
01:12:01,108 --> 01:12:03,025
How about showing us
a little leadership?

790
01:12:03,109 --> 01:12:05,069
Forget fucking Shirley Temple.
You take charge.

791
01:12:05,154 --> 01:12:07,404
- Right.
- You run things here anyway.

792
01:12:07,489 --> 01:12:12,493
No fuckin' way.
I'm not the officer type.

793
01:12:13,578 --> 01:12:15,747
I just take care of my own.

794
01:12:15,831 --> 01:12:19,042
Well, what does
this fucking beast want?

795
01:12:21,170 --> 01:12:23,087
Is this mother
gonna try for us all?

796
01:12:26,466 --> 01:12:29,051
- Yeah.
- Well, ain't that sweet?

797
01:12:29,136 --> 01:12:31,930
- So how are we gonna stop it?
- [ Clears Throat ]

798
01:12:35,475 --> 01:12:38,270
- We have no weapons.
Is that correct?
- Right.

799
01:12:38,354 --> 01:12:42,064
I haven't seen one
exactly like this before.

800
01:12:42,149 --> 01:12:44,609
Moves differently.

801
01:12:46,695 --> 01:12:49,197
But the others
were afraid of fire-

802
01:12:49,282 --> 01:12:51,283
not much else.

803
01:12:52,577 --> 01:12:55,744
- Can we seal off this area?
- No chance.

804
01:12:55,829 --> 01:12:57,997
The installation's 1 0 miles square.

805
01:12:58,123 --> 01:13:00,375
There's 600 air ducts
running to the surface.
What about video?

806
01:13:00,458 --> 01:13:04,170
I see these closed-circuit monitors everywhere.
We could try to find it that way.

807
01:13:04,255 --> 01:13:08,382
The video system hasn't worked in years.
Nothing much works here.

808
01:13:08,466 --> 01:13:10,676
We got a lot of technology,
no way to fix it.

809
01:13:10,761 --> 01:13:13,179
- What 85 is trying to tell you is-
- Don't call me that!

810
01:13:13,264 --> 01:13:16,349
we ain't got no entertainment center,
no climate control,

811
01:13:16,434 --> 01:13:19,019
no video system,
no surveillance,

812
01:13:19,103 --> 01:13:22,605
no freezers, no fucking ice cream,

813
01:13:22,689 --> 01:13:25,483
no rubbers, no women, no guns.

814
01:13:25,568 --> 01:13:27,652
All we got here is shit!

815
01:13:27,737 --> 01:13:30,447
Oh, what the hell are we
even talking to her for?

816
01:13:30,530 --> 01:13:33,949
She's the one
that brought the fucker.

817
01:13:34,034 --> 01:13:37,912
Why don't we just get her head
and shove it through the fucking wall?

818
01:13:37,997 --> 01:13:40,247
That sounds good to me.

819
01:13:40,332 --> 01:13:42,333
[ Dillon ]
Hey, Morse.

820
01:13:46,255 --> 01:13:48,381
Why don't you shut the fuck up?

821
01:13:49,550 --> 01:13:51,551
Hmm.

822
01:13:54,346 --> 01:13:56,347
Right.

823
01:13:57,350 --> 01:14:00,393
Right. What are we going to do?

824
01:14:14,824 --> 01:14:17,284
What's this?
Um,

825
01:14:17,369 --> 01:14:20,454
that leads from the mess hall
to the infirmary.

826
01:14:20,538 --> 01:14:22,539
It's a ventilation shaft.

827
01:14:22,625 --> 01:14:25,960
Then we go in there, flush it out.

828
01:14:26,045 --> 01:14:30,047
Hey. Hey, look, there's miles and miles
of tunnel through there.

829
01:14:31,050 --> 01:14:33,051
It won't go far.

830
01:14:34,095 --> 01:14:36,387
It'll nest in this area.

831
01:14:36,471 --> 01:14:38,472
Right around...

832
01:14:39,475 --> 01:14:42,976
here.
How do you know that?

833
01:14:44,229 --> 01:14:46,773
It's like a lion.

834
01:14:46,856 --> 01:14:49,067
It sticks close to the zebras.

835
01:14:49,150 --> 01:14:51,569
Zebras? Oh, right.

836
01:14:51,654 --> 01:14:54,322
But, look. Running around down here
in the dark- Are you kidding?

837
01:14:54,407 --> 01:14:56,783
Once you get out of this main shaft,
there's no overheads.

838
01:14:56,908 --> 01:15:00,036
Don't we have flashlights?
We got thousands of 'em,
but no batteries.

839
01:15:00,162 --> 01:15:02,956
I told you, nothing works.
Torches?

840
01:15:03,039 --> 01:15:06,042
Do we have the capacity
to make fire?

841
01:15:06,127 --> 01:15:09,421
Most humans have enjoyed that privilege
since the Stone Age.

842
01:15:10,506 --> 01:15:12,756
No need to be sarcastic.

843
01:15:14,510 --> 01:15:18,430
Never been used. They were gonna
dump a lot of nuclear crap in there.

844
01:15:18,514 --> 01:15:21,640
Never got around to it.
It's clean as a whistle inside.

845
01:15:21,725 --> 01:15:24,185
This the only way in or out?

846
01:15:24,270 --> 01:15:28,021
That's right. Walls are
six feet thick, solid steel.

847
01:15:28,106 --> 01:15:30,524
Really knew how
to build these babies.

848
01:15:30,609 --> 01:15:33,528
You're saying we get
something in there,

849
01:15:33,612 --> 01:15:36,072
there's no way it can get out?

850
01:15:36,157 --> 01:15:39,408
That's right. No fucking way.

851
01:15:43,122 --> 01:15:44,956
[ Whistles ]

852
01:15:46,375 --> 01:15:48,752
This is where we keep it.
I forget what the stuff's called.

853
01:15:48,836 --> 01:15:52,337
Quinitricetyline.
l knew that.

854
01:15:52,422 --> 01:15:55,675
Right. I've got to get these section
arrangements organized with Dillon...

855
01:15:55,760 --> 01:15:58,386
for the paintbrush, uh-

856
01:15:58,470 --> 01:16:00,846
So, um-
David.

857
01:16:00,972 --> 01:16:05,018
Yeah. You can get
these drums organized.
Right, 85.

858
01:16:05,101 --> 01:16:08,479
And, uh, don't call me that.

859
01:16:10,983 --> 01:16:14,903
What's this "85" thing?

860
01:16:14,987 --> 01:16:18,280
Couple of us sneaked a look at
his personnel file the day he arrived.

861
01:16:18,364 --> 01:16:20,365
lt's his I.Q.

862
01:16:27,500 --> 01:16:29,626
I saw a drum of this stuff...

863
01:16:29,710 --> 01:16:31,877
fall into a beachhead bunker once.

864
01:16:31,962 --> 01:16:35,422
The blast put a tug
in dry dock for 1 7 weeks.

865
01:16:35,507 --> 01:16:36,298
Great stuff!

866
01:16:42,055 --> 01:16:45,099
All right.
Let me get this straight.

867
01:16:45,184 --> 01:16:48,603
You want to burn it down
and out of the pipes,

868
01:16:48,686 --> 01:16:50,854
force it in here,
slam the door...

869
01:16:50,939 --> 01:16:53,565
and trap its ass?
Right.

870
01:16:53,650 --> 01:16:57,487
And you want help
from us y-chromo boys, huh?

871
01:16:57,570 --> 01:16:59,447
You got something better to do?

872
01:16:59,532 --> 01:17:02,324
Why should we put our ass
on the line for you?

873
01:17:02,408 --> 01:17:04,577
Your ass is already on the line.

874
01:17:04,662 --> 01:17:06,287
The only question is...

875
01:17:06,372 --> 01:17:08,789
what are you gonna do about it?

876
01:17:08,873 --> 01:17:12,042
[ Chattering ]

877
01:17:21,595 --> 01:17:23,595
Look at this.

878
01:17:23,680 --> 01:17:26,140
There's only one of these fucking batteries
in 2,000 that works.

879
01:17:26,266 --> 01:17:28,475
Hey, it could have been
a lot worse.
Yeah?

880
01:17:28,560 --> 01:17:33,105
We might have got
the paintbrush detail.

881
01:17:36,777 --> 01:17:38,860
Man, this stuff stinks.

882
01:17:52,458 --> 01:17:56,337
This shit smells awful.
Then don't breathe
the fucking fumes.

883
01:17:56,421 --> 01:17:59,381
I'm in a fucking pipe with it.
How can I keep from breathing it!

884
01:17:59,466 --> 01:18:02,719
I mean,
don't breathe too hard.

885
01:18:02,845 --> 01:18:06,264
You'll get high.
That's good for me.

886
01:18:14,773 --> 01:18:17,024
So you miss Doc, right?

887
01:18:19,737 --> 01:18:22,238
What makes you say that?

888
01:18:22,323 --> 01:18:24,657
I thought you two got real close.

889
01:18:24,742 --> 01:18:27,201
[ Sighs ]

890
01:18:27,286 --> 01:18:30,162
I guess you've been looking
through some keyholes.

891
01:18:30,288 --> 01:18:34,917
That's what I thought.
[ Exhales ]
Oh!

892
01:18:35,002 --> 01:18:37,002
Oh.

893
01:18:39,422 --> 01:18:43,134
- You okay?
- Yeah. l'm fine.

894
01:18:43,217 --> 01:18:47,805
Whatever you say, but, uh,
you don't look okay to me, sister.

895
01:18:49,475 --> 01:18:51,475
l'm fine.

896
01:18:55,021 --> 01:18:57,481
I hate this place.
I hate this place.

897
01:19:00,985 --> 01:19:02,944
Well.

898
01:19:03,029 --> 01:19:05,657
There's definitely
something in here with us.

899
01:19:07,951 --> 01:19:10,744
Okay. Don't light the fire
until I give the signal.

900
01:19:10,828 --> 01:19:13,413
This is the signal.

901
01:19:13,498 --> 01:19:16,833
Got it?
Can you remember that?

902
01:19:19,003 --> 01:19:21,130
[ Grunts ]

903
01:19:21,215 --> 01:19:23,006
[ Groans ]
Shit!

904
01:20:00,628 --> 01:20:03,088
[ Hissing ]

905
01:20:15,394 --> 01:20:18,061
[ Muttering ]
Buh-

906
01:20:23,609 --> 01:20:25,862
Wait for the fucking signal!

907
01:20:26,947 --> 01:20:27,613
[ No Audible Dialogue ]

908
01:20:34,078 --> 01:20:36,122
Get down!

909
01:20:37,207 --> 01:20:39,751
Aaah!

910
01:20:39,835 --> 01:20:43,296
Come on, come on!
We gotta find the sprinklers!

911
01:20:43,380 --> 01:20:45,547
Come on!
We gotta help these guys!

912
01:20:47,760 --> 01:20:50,261
[ Screaming ]

913
01:20:53,724 --> 01:20:56,100
Come on! Move! Move!

914
01:20:57,728 --> 01:21:00,313
Go to the waste dump.
Don't open the doors!

915
01:21:51,489 --> 01:21:55,158
[ Screaming ]

916
01:22:03,167 --> 01:22:05,043
Oh, God!
It's all right.

917
01:22:05,127 --> 01:22:08,506
It's all right. You're gonna be all right.
We got you.

918
01:22:09,550 --> 01:22:12,676
- Fire's out.
- [ Screaming Continues ]

919
01:22:22,395 --> 01:22:25,146
Junior! Junior!
Get those sprinklers and turn them on.

920
01:22:26,065 --> 01:22:28,693
We gotta get him out of here.

921
01:22:34,949 --> 01:22:37,702
Come on.
We're walking you out.

922
01:22:44,917 --> 01:22:48,212
Junior! Behind you!

923
01:22:50,381 --> 01:22:52,007
Open the door!

924
01:22:53,342 --> 01:22:55,386
Come on! Come on!

925
01:23:00,893 --> 01:23:02,935
[ Hisses ]

926
01:23:03,020 --> 01:23:05,896
Come on! Come on!

927
01:23:05,980 --> 01:23:07,523
Come and get me, fucker!

928
01:23:18,577 --> 01:23:20,703
[ Junior Screaming ]
[ Alien Screeching ]

929
01:23:21,829 --> 01:23:24,039
[ Panting ]

930
01:23:27,252 --> 01:23:29,753
[ Flesh Tearing ]
[ Screaming Continues ]

931
01:23:32,882 --> 01:23:34,800
[ Screaming Stops ]

932
01:23:49,149 --> 01:23:53,360
♪♪ [ Woman Vocalizing ]

933
01:24:41,326 --> 01:24:44,494
[ Dillon ]
Even for those who have fallen,

934
01:24:44,578 --> 01:24:48,416
this is a time of rejoicing.

935
01:24:49,751 --> 01:24:54,046
♪♪ [ Continues ]
We salute their courage.

936
01:24:54,131 --> 01:24:57,800
They will live forever.

937
01:25:01,220 --> 01:25:04,724
Those that are dead are not dead.

938
01:25:04,807 --> 01:25:07,600
They have moved up.

939
01:25:07,685 --> 01:25:11,354
They have moved to a higher place.

940
01:25:11,439 --> 01:25:14,149
Crazy bastards.

941
01:25:14,234 --> 01:25:18,069
Andrews used to call them Dillon's God Squad.
Keeps 'em out of mischief.

942
01:25:19,864 --> 01:25:22,615
- You're not the religious type.
- Me? [ Scoffs ]

943
01:25:22,701 --> 01:25:25,368
Shit, no. I've got a job.

944
01:25:26,704 --> 01:25:28,997
Look, uh-
[ Clears Throat ]

945
01:25:29,082 --> 01:25:32,042
Figure the rescue team gets here in
four, five days-

946
01:25:32,127 --> 01:25:34,252
six, tops.

947
01:25:34,337 --> 01:25:39,341
They open the door, go in there
with smart guns and kill it.

948
01:25:41,886 --> 01:25:45,722
What have you heard from them?
Nothing much.

949
01:25:45,806 --> 01:25:48,309
We got a message received.

950
01:25:48,393 --> 01:25:51,353
Later, we got something
that said you were top priority.

951
01:25:53,189 --> 01:25:55,356
They don't cut us in on much.

952
01:25:55,442 --> 01:25:58,652
We're the ass end of
the totem pole out here.

953
01:25:58,737 --> 01:26:00,945
What if they don't want to kill it?

954
01:26:03,074 --> 01:26:06,202
- Take it back?
- Yeah.

955
01:26:06,286 --> 01:26:10,538
They're not lunatics, you know?
Gotta kill it.

956
01:26:10,623 --> 01:26:12,750
Right?

957
01:26:18,506 --> 01:26:22,551
[ Golic ]
Morse, please, cut me loose.

958
01:26:22,636 --> 01:26:24,386
No fucking way.
[ Trimmer Buzzing ]

959
01:26:24,470 --> 01:26:26,137
Come on, man. It hurts.

960
01:26:26,264 --> 01:26:28,224
Oh, sorry.
[ Whimpering ]

961
01:26:28,307 --> 01:26:31,476
Come on. I haven't done nothing.

962
01:26:31,603 --> 01:26:36,148
Just don't talk to me.
Please, what did I do? Please.

963
01:26:36,233 --> 01:26:40,778
I'll tell you what I'm gonna do. I'm gonna sit
here and guard your ass like l'm supposed to.

964
01:26:40,862 --> 01:26:43,488
I don't need any
fucking trouble with Dillon.

965
01:26:43,573 --> 01:26:47,408
All I did was tell 'em about the dragon,
what it did to Boggs and Rains.

966
01:26:47,493 --> 01:26:51,122
I didn't lie. You saw it.

967
01:26:51,206 --> 01:26:53,082
Fuckin' "A" I saw it.

968
01:26:53,166 --> 01:26:55,583
Oh, please.
[ Whimpering ]

969
01:26:55,668 --> 01:26:58,671
If this gets in here,
I'm dead. I can't run.

970
01:26:58,755 --> 01:27:00,797
It's not going to get in here.
We got it trapped.

971
01:27:04,552 --> 01:27:07,595
So what's the big deal?
Come on. Let me loose, man.

972
01:27:09,515 --> 01:27:14,185
Don't I always
give you cigarettes first?
Yeah.

973
01:27:14,311 --> 01:27:17,273
Aren't I your friend?
[ Clicks Off ]

974
01:27:17,356 --> 01:27:22,319
- I love you, Morse.
- [ Trimmer Clatters ]

975
01:27:23,488 --> 01:27:25,905
Why not?

976
01:27:30,828 --> 01:27:33,329
But behave yourself.
No fucking around...

977
01:27:33,414 --> 01:27:35,875
or I'll get nothing but shit.

978
01:27:44,091 --> 01:27:47,511
- So where they got it?
- [ Chuckles ]
In the waste tank.

979
01:27:47,636 --> 01:27:52,307
[ Clicks On ]
We got that sucker nailed.
I mean, tight.

980
01:27:52,391 --> 01:27:54,935
Gotta see it again.

981
01:27:55,020 --> 01:27:56,895
What the fuck you talking about?

982
01:27:59,899 --> 01:28:02,775
No more cigarettes for you.

983
01:28:02,860 --> 01:28:06,613
[ Typing ]

984
01:28:10,452 --> 01:28:14,579
Right. We got the first part.
Now what do we say?

985
01:28:14,706 --> 01:28:18,042
Tell them we trapped it.
[ Beeps ]

986
01:28:18,167 --> 01:28:22,296
What do we call it?
A xenomorph.

987
01:28:22,380 --> 01:28:24,381
Right.

988
01:28:25,382 --> 01:28:28,469
[ Clears Throat ]
How do you spell it?

989
01:28:28,552 --> 01:28:31,055
Here.

990
01:28:34,059 --> 01:28:36,018
[ Typing ]

991
01:28:45,612 --> 01:28:47,238
Hey, wait a minute.
We can't kill it.

992
01:28:47,363 --> 01:28:49,030
We don't have
any weapons, right?
Right.

993
01:28:53,203 --> 01:28:57,247
See? That's all they ever tell us.
Treat us like shit.

994
01:29:09,927 --> 01:29:12,930
[ Breathing Loudly ]

995
01:29:23,524 --> 01:29:26,568
- Off and on me now?
- What the hell you talking about?

996
01:29:26,653 --> 01:29:29,238
Talk to me, the beast.

997
01:29:29,322 --> 01:29:34,702
You can't go in there, dickhead.
The big mothersucker will eat you alive.

998
01:29:44,087 --> 01:29:46,671
Sorry.
[ Gasps ]

999
01:29:46,756 --> 01:29:49,800
Sorry, sorry, sorry,
sorry, sorry.

1000
01:29:58,726 --> 01:30:01,936
♪♪ [ Woman Vocalizing ]

1001
01:30:15,034 --> 01:30:17,036
Tell me what to do next.

1002
01:30:18,496 --> 01:30:22,832
♪♪ [ Vocalizing Continues ]

1003
01:30:41,101 --> 01:30:42,853
[ Bones Crunching ]

1004
01:30:46,190 --> 01:30:48,984
So, you're telling me they're coming to
take this thing away?

1005
01:30:49,069 --> 01:30:52,363
Yeah, they're gonna try.
They don't wanna kill it.

1006
01:30:52,447 --> 01:30:54,948
We gotta figure out a way to do it
before they come here.

1007
01:30:55,033 --> 01:30:59,078
Why do we have to kill it?
You just said the company's coming for it.

1008
01:30:59,162 --> 01:31:02,206
That's right.
They wanna take it back.

1009
01:31:02,289 --> 01:31:05,083
Some sort of weapon.
Yeah, what's wrong with that?

1010
01:31:05,167 --> 01:31:07,502
They can't control it.
They don't understand. It'll kill them all.

1011
01:31:08,837 --> 01:31:10,671
Like I said,
what's wrong with that?

1012
01:31:10,756 --> 01:31:15,094
Nothing's wrong with that...
except a lot of innocent people will die.

1013
01:31:18,847 --> 01:31:21,850
[ Sighs ]
I thought you were
a religious man.

1014
01:31:21,935 --> 01:31:24,560
You don't understand, do you?

1015
01:31:26,439 --> 01:31:30,609
That world out there
doesn't exist for us anymore.

1016
01:31:31,735 --> 01:31:34,488
We've got our own
little world out here.

1017
01:31:34,572 --> 01:31:38,242
It ain't much, but it's ours.

1018
01:31:38,326 --> 01:31:42,121
So fuck everybody else.

1019
01:31:42,204 --> 01:31:45,916
No. Fuck them.

1020
01:31:48,420 --> 01:31:50,503
- Hey, Dillon?
- Yeah?

1021
01:31:52,756 --> 01:31:57,594
Uh, Dillon, we got
a teeny-weeny problem.

1022
01:32:13,110 --> 01:32:16,320
[ Aaron ]
Fucking great!

1023
01:32:16,405 --> 01:32:20,033
Miserable, crazy
son of a bitch let him loose.

1024
01:32:20,118 --> 01:32:21,784
Got what he fucking deserved.

1025
01:32:23,121 --> 01:32:26,038
[ Exhales ]
Well, now what are we gonna do?

1026
01:32:26,123 --> 01:32:30,335
Andrews was right.
Should've kept the shithead chained up.

1027
01:32:30,420 --> 01:32:34,756
- [ Gasps ]
- You okay?

1028
01:32:34,882 --> 01:32:38,051
Piss on her.
The fucking thing's loose out there.
What are we gonna do?

1029
01:32:38,136 --> 01:32:40,761
l just said that.

1030
01:32:40,846 --> 01:32:44,891
And you're the dumb prick that let Golic out.
You miserable little shit!

1031
01:32:44,975 --> 01:32:46,685
Come on. Cut that shit out.

1032
01:32:46,810 --> 01:32:51,023
Tell your fucking bozo to shape up!
[ Gasping ]

1033
01:32:51,106 --> 01:32:53,399
Wh-Wh-What do you think?

1034
01:32:53,484 --> 01:32:55,652
[ Exhales ]
I think I have
to get to the E.E.V.

1035
01:32:55,737 --> 01:32:59,864
- Why? What's up?
- I just have to use the neuroscanner.

1036
01:33:01,493 --> 01:33:03,618
- You don't look so good.
- Who gives a shit how she looks?

1037
01:33:03,703 --> 01:33:07,413
- What are we gonna do?
- Want a smack in the mouth,
you stupid wanker?

1038
01:33:07,498 --> 01:33:09,416
Shut the fuck up
and stop causing panic!

1039
01:33:09,501 --> 01:33:12,961
Panic- You're so fucking stupid,
you couldn't spell it.
Don't talk to me about panic.

1040
01:33:13,087 --> 01:33:15,463
We ought to panic!
We're fucking screwed!
Whose fault is that?

1041
01:33:15,547 --> 01:33:17,507
All right.
Now shut up, both of you!

1042
01:33:19,594 --> 01:33:21,677
Shut up!

1043
01:33:37,987 --> 01:33:41,155
- Well, I'm out of ideas!
- Oh, surprise me.

1044
01:33:43,534 --> 01:33:46,036
What about outside?
Great idea.

1045
01:33:46,119 --> 01:33:48,454
Sun don't come up
for another two days.
It's 40 below zero.

1046
01:33:48,539 --> 01:33:51,166
The rescue team's 1 0 hours away.
So that makes a lot of sense!

1047
01:33:51,251 --> 01:33:54,586
Wonderful. You just want us to stay here
and let this thing have us for lunch!

1048
01:33:54,671 --> 01:33:58,297
I want you to get everybody
that's still left together.

1049
01:33:58,382 --> 01:34:02,636
Get 'em into the assembly hall.

1050
01:34:02,720 --> 01:34:04,887
Okay.

1051
01:34:08,059 --> 01:34:10,018
Where'd she go?

1052
01:34:12,771 --> 01:34:14,814
[ Switches Clicking ]

1053
01:34:36,796 --> 01:34:40,673
- Need any help?
- [ Exhales ]

1054
01:34:40,757 --> 01:34:44,677
I don't mean to scare you.

1055
01:34:44,761 --> 01:34:47,096
You shouldn't be
wandering around alone.

1056
01:34:47,180 --> 01:34:50,350
Do me a favor and run
this keyboard, will you?

1057
01:34:52,185 --> 01:34:53,854
Okay.

1058
01:35:04,323 --> 01:35:06,533
What do I do?
Hit "B" or "C."

1059
01:35:06,618 --> 01:35:08,284
What's "C"?

1060
01:35:08,411 --> 01:35:10,078
"Display biofunctions."
That's it.

1061
01:35:12,039 --> 01:35:13,832
[ Electrical Pulses ]

1062
01:35:13,916 --> 01:35:16,585
Okay, we're hot. Now what?

1063
01:35:16,668 --> 01:35:19,253
Let it run a cycle.

1064
01:35:19,338 --> 01:35:21,465
[ Aaron ]
It's real fuzzy.

1065
01:35:21,548 --> 01:35:24,635
Hit "enhancement."

1066
01:35:27,555 --> 01:35:29,805
[ Pulsing Continues ]

1067
01:35:40,652 --> 01:35:42,985
[ Sighs ]

1068
01:35:43,070 --> 01:35:44,988
Keep looking.

1069
01:35:52,287 --> 01:35:54,206
I don't know how to read this stuff.

1070
01:35:54,289 --> 01:35:57,792
[ Ripley ]
Hemorrhaging will show as a dark patch.

1071
01:36:03,466 --> 01:36:06,051
[ Clears Throat ]
Look for...

1072
01:36:06,135 --> 01:36:08,970
hairline fractures
through the base of the skull.

1073
01:36:09,096 --> 01:36:11,222
[ Electrical Drone ]
Little white lines.

1074
01:36:19,481 --> 01:36:21,399
What is it?

1075
01:36:23,194 --> 01:36:24,985
I think you've got one inside of you.

1076
01:36:27,030 --> 01:36:29,865
That's not possible.

1077
01:36:32,619 --> 01:36:35,037
[ Panting ]
What does it look like?

1078
01:36:39,585 --> 01:36:43,587
- Horrible.
- I have to see it.

1079
01:36:46,134 --> 01:36:48,051
- Freeze it.
- You don't want to look at it.

1080
01:36:48,136 --> 01:36:50,052
Freeze it!

1081
01:36:52,055 --> 01:36:53,890
[ Beeping ]

1082
01:37:15,537 --> 01:37:17,706
l'm sorry.

1083
01:37:22,545 --> 01:37:25,838
All right. The fucking thing is loose.
It's out there.

1084
01:37:25,922 --> 01:37:29,301
A rescue team is on its way
with guns and shit.

1085
01:37:29,385 --> 01:37:31,886
Right now there isn't
any place that's real safe.

1086
01:37:33,305 --> 01:37:35,265
But we stay here,
in the assembly hall.

1087
01:37:35,349 --> 01:37:38,435
This place never had
any fucking air conditioning.

1088
01:37:38,519 --> 01:37:40,729
If it comes in, it's gotta be through
one of these doors.

1089
01:37:40,813 --> 01:37:43,689
Now we post a guard
to let us know if it's coming.

1090
01:37:43,774 --> 01:37:49,029
In the meantime,
you lay low, be ready and stay right...

1091
01:37:49,113 --> 01:37:51,448
in case your time comes.

1092
01:37:51,532 --> 01:37:56,703
Don't you start bullshitting, Dillon.

1093
01:37:56,787 --> 01:37:58,788
We're gonna be
trapped in here like rats.

1094
01:37:58,872 --> 01:38:02,626
You got a weapon? You got a blade?
Then you take it out and you fucking use it!

1095
01:38:02,710 --> 01:38:07,463
Oh, right. So you think we're gonna
stab this mothersucker to death?

1096
01:38:07,547 --> 01:38:10,216
No, I don't think shit! Maybe.

1097
01:38:10,301 --> 01:38:13,220
Maybe you'll hurt it
before it takes you out, huh?

1098
01:38:13,304 --> 01:38:16,680
Isn't that something?
Any of you got any better ideas?

1099
01:38:22,063 --> 01:38:26,483
And I'll tell you, until the rescue team
gets here, we're fucked!

1100
01:38:28,152 --> 01:38:31,154
So you better get prepared.

1101
01:38:38,496 --> 01:38:40,956
Well, I ain't staying here.

1102
01:38:42,707 --> 01:38:45,335
Well, then, suit yourself.

1103
01:38:51,676 --> 01:38:53,510
Fire.

1104
01:38:57,974 --> 01:39:02,810
- Furnace.
- Yeah. Let's make it to the furnace.

1105
01:39:04,980 --> 01:39:07,983
Holy shit.

1106
01:39:09,318 --> 01:39:11,903
Well, all right.

1107
01:39:11,988 --> 01:39:14,072
Fuckin' "A."

1108
01:39:14,155 --> 01:39:17,492
- Fuckin' "A."
- Too fuckin' right it's right.

1109
01:39:35,552 --> 01:39:39,139
It's up. What do you want to say?

1110
01:39:40,725 --> 01:39:42,559
Tell them the whole place
has gone toxic.

1111
01:39:42,643 --> 01:39:45,353
Are you kidding?

1112
01:39:45,438 --> 01:39:47,898
Then they won't come here.
The rescue team will turn back.

1113
01:39:48,024 --> 01:39:50,567
Yeah. I know.
What are you talking about?

1114
01:39:50,650 --> 01:39:54,487
Our only hope is that
they kill this fucker.

1115
01:39:54,572 --> 01:39:57,823
And maybe they can do something for you.
I don't know, freeze you-

1116
01:39:57,908 --> 01:40:00,243
They can do an operation.
They've got the technology.

1117
01:40:00,328 --> 01:40:04,122
If this organism gets off the planet,
it'll kill everything.

1118
01:40:04,206 --> 01:40:06,498
The company doesn't care about that.

1119
01:40:06,583 --> 01:40:09,543
They just want it for
their bioweapons division, okay?

1120
01:40:09,628 --> 01:40:13,340
So we can't let them come here.

1121
01:40:13,423 --> 01:40:15,507
Fuck you.

1122
01:40:15,592 --> 01:40:19,345
Look, I'm sorry you've got this thing
inside you, but l'm getting rescued.

1123
01:40:19,430 --> 01:40:22,849
I don't give a shit about these
stupid prisoners, but l've got a wife, a kid.

1124
01:40:22,934 --> 01:40:25,935
- I'll go home on the next rotation!
- I know. This is hard.

1125
01:40:26,020 --> 01:40:29,689
I'm gonna send this message.
I need that fucking code.

1126
01:40:29,774 --> 01:40:32,775
I'm sorry, babe. It's classified.

1127
01:40:32,859 --> 01:40:35,654
Listen, you stupid little shit!
This has got to be done, okay?

1128
01:40:35,779 --> 01:40:38,198
There are no alternatives!
No way!

1129
01:40:38,282 --> 01:40:41,368
You're not getting it!
No fucking way!

1130
01:40:43,537 --> 01:40:45,454
[ Computer Beeps ]

1131
01:40:47,875 --> 01:40:50,042
Look, it's nothing personal.

1132
01:40:50,127 --> 01:40:52,628
Understand?

1133
01:40:52,712 --> 01:40:54,797
I think you're okay.

1134
01:40:55,800 --> 01:40:57,716
Ah.
[ Chuckles ]

1135
01:41:00,136 --> 01:41:01,637
Thanks.

1136
01:41:10,146 --> 01:41:13,524
- Have you got any ideas?
- [ Exhales ]

1137
01:41:13,609 --> 01:41:18,238
It won't kill me.

1138
01:41:18,322 --> 01:41:20,739
I'm carrying the new queen.

1139
01:41:20,824 --> 01:41:23,993
It won't kill its future.

1140
01:41:24,119 --> 01:41:28,914
You really wanna bet
this thing's that smart?
[ Clears Throat ]

1141
01:41:28,998 --> 01:41:33,502
Maybe I'll go find it.
See how smart it is.

1142
01:41:33,628 --> 01:41:36,922
You're gonna go
and look for it?
Yeah.

1143
01:41:37,006 --> 01:41:40,592
I have a pretty good idea
of where it is.

1144
01:41:40,677 --> 01:41:45,640
It's just down there... in the basement.

1145
01:41:45,765 --> 01:41:49,310
This whole place is a basement.
[ Chuckles ]

1146
01:41:49,395 --> 01:41:54,064
It's a metaphor. Wanna come?

1147
01:41:56,860 --> 01:42:01,989
[ Exhales ]
Fuck me.
[ Computer Beeping ]

1148
01:42:56,086 --> 01:42:59,546
[ Breathing Heavily ]

1149
01:42:59,631 --> 01:43:02,884
[ Gas Hisses ]
[ Clattering ]

1150
01:43:11,268 --> 01:43:13,310
[ Exhales Sharply ]

1151
01:43:22,613 --> 01:43:24,447
Where are you when I need you?

1152
01:43:28,786 --> 01:43:31,787
[ Clattering ]
[ Hissing ]

1153
01:43:43,967 --> 01:43:45,969
[ Exhales ]

1154
01:43:50,890 --> 01:43:53,768
[ Liquid Gurgling ]

1155
01:43:57,146 --> 01:43:59,399
Don't be afraid.

1156
01:44:01,609 --> 01:44:03,610
l'm part of the family.

1157
01:44:32,307 --> 01:44:34,725
[ Clattering ]

1158
01:45:10,637 --> 01:45:13,680
You've been in my life so long,

1159
01:45:13,765 --> 01:45:16,309
I can't remember anything else.

1160
01:45:18,561 --> 01:45:20,688
Now do something for me.

1161
01:45:22,524 --> 01:45:24,484
It's easy.

1162
01:45:24,568 --> 01:45:27,362
Just-

1163
01:45:27,445 --> 01:45:30,280
Just do what you do.

1164
01:45:30,365 --> 01:45:31,865
[ Grunts ]

1165
01:45:37,206 --> 01:45:39,623
[ Metal Clatters ]

1166
01:45:55,682 --> 01:45:58,559
[ Squealing ]

1167
01:45:59,645 --> 01:46:01,770
[ Hisses ]

1168
01:46:04,984 --> 01:46:07,402
Oh!
[ Thuds ]

1169
01:46:14,534 --> 01:46:18,412
- It won't kill me.
- What are you doing out here?
You're supposed to be laying low.

1170
01:46:18,497 --> 01:46:22,082
I have one inside of me.

1171
01:46:22,167 --> 01:46:23,792
Big one won't kill its own.

1172
01:46:23,918 --> 01:46:27,046
What are you talking about?
I just saw it,

1173
01:46:27,131 --> 01:46:29,798
an hour ago.

1174
01:46:29,882 --> 01:46:32,260
I stood right next to it.

1175
01:46:32,344 --> 01:46:36,346
I could've been lunch,
but it wouldn't touch me.

1176
01:46:36,431 --> 01:46:38,975
It ran away.

1177
01:46:40,101 --> 01:46:42,353
It knows I'm carrying its future.

1178
01:46:42,438 --> 01:46:45,605
Aw, bullshit. How do you know
that thing's inside you?

1179
01:46:45,690 --> 01:46:49,277
I saw it... on the CAT scan.

1180
01:46:49,360 --> 01:46:54,448
It's a queen- an egg layer.

1181
01:46:54,533 --> 01:46:56,533
It can make thousands more
like the one we've got here.

1182
01:46:56,618 --> 01:47:00,328
Still sounds like bullshit to me.

1183
01:47:00,413 --> 01:47:03,291
If that thing's inside you,
how'd it get there?

1184
01:47:03,375 --> 01:47:07,587
[ Exhales ]
I don't know.

1185
01:47:07,671 --> 01:47:10,088
When I was in hypersleep, I guess.

1186
01:47:10,173 --> 01:47:12,382
l was violated.

1187
01:47:14,136 --> 01:47:16,804
Now I get to be the mother.

1188
01:47:20,266 --> 01:47:23,935
I don't have much time,

1189
01:47:24,020 --> 01:47:27,355
and I can't do what I should.

1190
01:47:29,818 --> 01:47:31,819
I need you to help me.

1191
01:47:35,364 --> 01:47:38,408
I need you to kill me.

1192
01:47:38,493 --> 01:47:42,121
- What the fuck are you talking about?
- I'm dead anyway.

1193
01:47:42,206 --> 01:47:45,792
I can't survive it.

1194
01:47:45,876 --> 01:47:48,877
But the one inside of me
can generate thousands more,

1195
01:47:50,631 --> 01:47:53,423
can wipe out the whole universe.

1196
01:47:53,509 --> 01:47:56,010
lt has to die.

1197
01:47:56,095 --> 01:47:58,554
So somebody's gotta kill me.

1198
01:48:01,140 --> 01:48:03,184
Are you up to it?

1199
01:48:04,228 --> 01:48:07,229
You don't have to worry about that.

1200
01:48:18,658 --> 01:48:20,743
[ Exhales ]

1201
01:48:24,747 --> 01:48:26,791
No speeches.

1202
01:48:30,002 --> 01:48:32,255
No prayers.

1203
01:48:48,771 --> 01:48:50,939
[ Exhales, Sniffs ]

1204
01:49:03,619 --> 01:49:06,204
- What's going on?
- I don't like losing a fight.

1205
01:49:06,289 --> 01:49:08,498
[ Metal Clatters ]
Not to nobody, not to nothing.

1206
01:49:08,625 --> 01:49:13,087
Fuck.
That damn thing out there
has already killed half my men,

1207
01:49:13,171 --> 01:49:15,006
got the other half scared shitless.

1208
01:49:15,090 --> 01:49:18,176
As long as it's alive, sister,
you're not gonna save any universe.

1209
01:49:18,260 --> 01:49:19,886
[ Softly ]
You said you were gonna kill me.

1210
01:49:19,970 --> 01:49:24,140
- You fucking coward!
- I want that thing!

1211
01:49:24,224 --> 01:49:27,726
I want to get this thing,
and I need you to do it.

1212
01:49:27,810 --> 01:49:31,980
And if it won't kill you,
then maybe that helps us fight it.

1213
01:49:32,106 --> 01:49:35,984
Otherwise, fuck you!
[ Groans ]

1214
01:49:36,110 --> 01:49:39,113
[ Whimpering ]
Go kill yourself.

1215
01:49:43,118 --> 01:49:45,493
[ Metal Scrapes ]
Dillon.

1216
01:49:46,872 --> 01:49:48,706
We waste this thing,

1217
01:49:50,542 --> 01:49:52,667
then you take care of me.
No problem.

1218
01:49:54,003 --> 01:49:57,672
Quick, easy and painless.

1219
01:50:02,261 --> 01:50:04,596
This is the choice.

1220
01:50:04,680 --> 01:50:08,600
You die sitting here on your ass,
or you die out there.

1221
01:50:08,685 --> 01:50:12,270
At least we take a shot.
We owe it one.

1222
01:50:12,355 --> 01:50:16,775
It's fucked us up.
Maybe we can get even for the others.

1223
01:50:18,069 --> 01:50:20,779
- Now how do you want it?
- What the fuck are you talking about?

1224
01:50:20,863 --> 01:50:23,490
I'm talkin' about killing
that big motherfucker.

1225
01:50:23,574 --> 01:50:26,827
Hold it, hold it.
The rescue team's on its way.

1226
01:50:26,912 --> 01:50:30,163
We could just sit this out.

1227
01:50:30,248 --> 01:50:33,042
- [ Ripley ]
Rescue team for whom?
- For us.

1228
